{"title":"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bank employee is filling an empty cash machine with bundles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce3da6473208f0e7595cbdac956b7abd66b8aad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be68b67793eb8fb9df7111777d94b145767394b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$10.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee8b158a4831195dbf4827a2edf8b53e5fbfec95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$20.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> bills. Each bundle has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> bills in it and the machine holds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> bundles of each type. What amount of money is required to fill the machine?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/97480c8eecf411853aaca35d16f68512b01c23f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\$30~000 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\$25~000 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\$35~000 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\$40~000 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\$45~000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"643\" height=\"19\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each bundle has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> bills of each type of bill, we can calculate the amount of money in each type of bundle first.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/7/1470a033bebd27606f25773d611052a0d8435667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5.00 \\times 100 = \\$500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" />, so each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce3da6473208f0e7595cbdac956b7abd66b8aad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> dollar bundle will be worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/6/ea6fbe7798f1b862bb683350572b65fa6a30d684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> dollars.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b27d7c77efb5d4c8121d6fcee3039b25741855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10.00 \\times 100 = \\$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"162\" height=\"17\" />, so each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be68b67793eb8fb9df7111777d94b145767394b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$10.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> dollar bundle will be worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805d460c4bb0ab7827844b0c21ff4c9b8ae17304.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> dollars.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4a564e782c347926606f2794719b770b9dedef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20.00 \\times 100 = \\$2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"162\" height=\"17\" />, so each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee8b158a4831195dbf4827a2edf8b53e5fbfec95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$20.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> dollar bundle will be worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d50502cbce1894e06cd3f7651e7f33c87380065f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> dollars.\n</p><p>Since the machine can hold <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> bundles of each type, we can add these together and multiply it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to get the total value needed to completely fill the machine:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f912c3b8473b7998bb3595aa17406c86f253f712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\times (\\$500 + \\$1000 + \\$2000) = 10 \\times \\$3500 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\$35~000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"469\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/